# Security headers for the Render static site.
#
# connect-src lists BOTH backends deliberately, rather than one per branch.
#
# This file previously named only the staging backend, on every branch. Staging
# served exactly that; production served the production backend. So production's
# real policy lived solely in the Render dashboard and the file committed here
# was wrong for it. Anyone recreating the production static site from this
# repository would have shipped a CSP pointing at staging, which blocks every
# API call the app makes - a total outage with no server-side error to diagnose.
#
# Naming both origins keeps one correct file for both environments, so a
# staging -> main merge can never carry the wrong value across. It is not the
# access-control boundary and does not need to be: which backend a page talks
# to is decided by the API_BASE hostname map in the app itself, and each backend
# independently rejects foreign origins through its own CORS_ORIGINS allowlist.
# CSP here is a backstop against exfiltration to an unrelated host, and both of
# these hosts are ours.
#
# When a custom domain is added, add its backend origin here in the same commit
# that configures it.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://athwa-backend-943m.onrender.com https://athwa-backend-staging.onrender.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'
